A component declared inside a body, on every target. The declaration binds in
the body's scope and nowhere else; what a backend emits is what it emits for a
top-level component, because passNoInlineComponents substitutes both into their
callers and neither survives as a host declaration.

Two bodies each declare their own, and one of them shadows the top-level `card`
that the sibling `other` still resolves to -- the golden is where "shadows in
one body only" is visible as two different strings in the output.

Before this, a bodyless `row(label="a")` resolved the component from the
package root (ir.SymbolTable.LookupComponent), so a body-local declaration was
never found: the node reached codegen as an ir.CallStmt with no Component and
every target emitted nothing for it, silently.

deny * `renderRow` -- nothing survives as a host component, so no target emits a render member for one

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
    none {
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

component card(label = "") {
    text(value="top " + label)
}

component other() {
    card(label="y")
}

component first() {
    component row(label = "") {
        text(value="row " + label)
    }

    row(label="a")
}

component main {
    component card(label = "") {
        text(value="inner " + label)
    }

    vbox {
        first()
        card(label="x")
        other()
    }
}
